### Short bio

I started my first business at 17 and spent 28 years building and running multiple businesses before I coached anyone. I know what it feels like to carry a business on your shoulders when nobody else is going to sort it. For the last 8 years I have worked specifically with MDs of groundworks, civils and allied trades businesses in Yorkshire, helping them find where the margin goes and build a team that stops depending on them for every decision. I was ranked the world's number one business coach four years running. What that means in practice: my clients get results they can point at, not folders they never open.

### One-line introduction

Pam Woodford is a Hull-based business coach who helps MDs of construction and allied trades businesses in Yorkshire keep more of what they earn and stop sorting everything themselves.

### For partners and events

Pam Woodford started her first business at 17 and spent 28 years building and running multiple service and retail businesses before she coached anyone. She has spent the last 8 years working specifically with MDs of groundworks, civils, drainage and allied trades businesses across Yorkshire, helping them find where the margin leaks and build teams that stop depending on the owner for every decision. She was ranked the world's number one business coach four years running, from 2015 to 2018, measured on client results. She is based in Hull, she is plain-spoken, and she has no patience for theory that does not show up in the bank account.

> **Number needed: John Davy result:** The John Davy testimonial is strong but stops short of a usable proof stat. To make it 'Ready', add one or more of the following: the approximate profit figure or percentage improvement Pam identified across his companies, the timeframe of the coaching relationship, and the number of companies involved. Ask John directly, or check session notes for a number he has shared. Even a range ('six figures of profit identified across three businesses in 18 months') turns this from a quote into a proof point.

===== story:onepager (29s, 4047 chars)
Pam Woodford is a Hull-based business coach who has run her own businesses since age 17 and spent the last 8 years working specifically with MDs of construction and allied trades businesses across Yorkshire. She helps owners who are winning decent work but not keeping enough of it find where the margin goes and build a team that stops depending on them for every decision.

- **43 years** Running and building businesses, starting at age 17
- **#1 globally** Ranked world's number one business coach four years running: 2015, 2016, 2017 and 2018
- **8 years** Working specifically with MDs in construction and allied trades

### Who I help

My core client is the MD of a groundworks, civils, drainage or allied trades business in Yorkshire. Typically 12 to 35 staff, £1.5M to £8M in turnover, and a business built over 10 to 20 years of hard graft. From the outside, everything looks fine. Behind the scenes, the margin keeps disappearing between pricing the job and finishing it, every decision still lands on his phone, and the bank account at month-end does not reflect the turnover going through. He is brilliant at the trade. The business just is not paying him back the way it should.

### The problems I fix

- The margin looked alright when I priced it but by the time we finished there was next to nowt in it.
- I'm still doing half my contracts manager's job because it's quicker to sort it myself.
- We're putting through nearly three million quid this year. Where the hell has it gone?
- I know the business isn't quite right. I just don't know which bit to fix first. Or if I've got time to fix anything.

### How I work

1. **The BOSS Scorecard.** Before we have a single conversation, the MD completes the BOSS Profit and Performance Scorecard. It takes three minutes and shows exactly which area is capping the business right now. The work starts on his numbers, not a standard programme.
2. **Weekly sessions to find the quick wins.** The first four to six weeks are weekly. We look at the five profit levers in his business: margin, pricing, team structure, cash flow and pipeline. We find where the money is leaking and fix the most painful thing first. Most owners free up hours in the first few weeks rather than adding to their load.
3. **Twice a month, ongoing.** Once the quick wins are in, we move to two 90-minute sessions a month. Direct access between sessions. Accountability on what was agreed. No worksheets he will not use. The relationship is built to last as long as the business does.

### Results

- John Davy, business owner: 'I believe that Pam is the best coach I have ever, ever had. Specifically I can point to huge amounts of profit in my various companies that Pam and only Pam recognised. Her fees are completely outstripped by the money that you will get back.'
- Guided over 250 licensed business coaches as Head of Coach Results and Director of Coaching Excellence at Business Coach Academy, measured on the results they delivered for clients.
- Ranked world's number one business coach four consecutive years, 2015 to 2018, measured on client results and business growth delivered.

### Working together

The best introduction is an MD of a construction or allied trades business in Yorkshire who is winning decent work but wondering where the money goes. Accountants, solicitors, plant hire companies, main contractors and trade associations are the people most likely to know him. He is not looking for a coach. He is looking for someone who understands the trade, will sit down with his numbers, and will help him keep more of what he earns without another year of the same graft. If a client of yours is carrying the whole business on their shoulders and the business is not paying them back the way it should, it is worth a conversation. Introducing them costs nothing. Finding the margin they are leaving behind often changes everything.

- **LinkedIn:** linkedin.com/in/theprofitcoach
- **Website:** theprofitcoach.com/pam
- **Email:** pam@theprofitcoach.com
- **Location:** Hull, Yorkshire

