### If they say not now

Don't push. Don't handle the objection. Just say: 'No problem at all, Steve. The main thing is you've got a clearer picture of where to focus.' Then send a short written note within 24 hours - two or three plain sentences summarising the one or two things you spotted in the session, and what they are worth acting on. No brochure, no follow-up sequence, no pressure. Close with: 'If it would be useful, I'm happy to check in with you in a couple of weeks and see how you're getting on.' Then do that. One short message, two weeks later. Most of the MDs who say not now are not saying no. They are saying not yet. Treat them accordingly.
